{'symbol': 'VRSK', 'date': '2022-03-23 20:00:00', 'title': 'VERISK ESTIMATES INSURED INDUSTRY LOSSES FOR M7.3 NAMIE, JAPAN, EARTHQUAKE', 'text': 'BOSTON, MARCH 23, 2022 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- ACCORDING TO VERISK EXTREME EVENT SOLUTIONS (FORMERLY AIR WORLDWIDE), INSURED LOSSES TO PROPERTIES FROM THE MARCH 16 M7.3 EARTHQUAKE THAT STRUCK OFFSHORE THE ISLAND OF HONSHU, JAPAN, WILL BE BETWEEN JPY 240 BILLION (~USD 2 BILLION) AND JPY 490 BILLION (~USD 4 BILLION). OF THAT, BETWEEN JPY 50 BILLION (~USD 400 MILLION) AND JPY 100 BILLION (~USD 820 MILLION) CAN BE ATTRIBUTED TO COMMERCIAL AND INDUSTRIAL PROPERTIES.'}